  "description": "The CELOS is our definition of the ideal short-travel bike: agile, playful to ride and efficient. For Alexander Kopp, it is the ideal bike for ultra-endurance races like the Silk Road Mountain Race; for us, it is the fastest bike for the after-work ride. The frame is built as a seamless monocoque from the highest-grade prepreg in an autoclave process, which makes it extremely light. The latest SUPERLIGHT layup version includes practical features such as the large storage compartment and the tool mount. The CELOS features durable bearings and is based on our robust frame platform, approved for ASTM Category 5: by swapping the rocker, it can be converted into an ASCO, CINTO or TARVO. You can configure your bike or frameset individually online. We are happy to advise you by phone, by email or in person in Dortmund, where you can also test ride all our bikes. To ensure this service and the quality of our frames, we limit the CELOS to 100 units per year.",
